<article class="env-corollary" id="2A7E5F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2A7E5F">Corollary <span data-tag="2A7E5F">4.4.2.5</span>.</a> Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ be a functor between $\infty $-categories. Assume that $\calC $ has all finite colimits. Then $f$ preserves all finite colimits if and only if $f$ preserves initial objects and pushouts. </p>
